meta {
  name: Follow a short code
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/{{linkCode}}
  body: none
  auth: none
}

settings {
  encodeUrl: true
  followRedirects: false
}

tests {
  test("answers 302 Found, never 301 (D8, FR-016)", function () {
    // A 301 is cached by the browser forever, which would break destination
    // editing for exactly the visitors who clicked before the edit.
    expect(res.getStatus()).to.equal(302);
  });

  test("sends the visitor to the current destination", function () {
    expect(res.getHeader("location")).to.equal("https://example.com/Hello?utm_source=poster");
  });

  test("forbids caching the mapping", function () {
    expect(res.getHeader("cache-control")).to.equal("no-store");
  });

  test("sets no cookie — the visitor is not the product (FR-015, Principle V)", function () {
    expect(res.getHeader("set-cookie")).to.be.undefined;
  });

  test("sends an empty body — the visitor is not meant to stop here", function () {
    expect(res.body).to.be.empty;
  });
}

docs {
  The public redirect surface, and the path Principle I calls sacred. It reads
  no credential of any kind, sets no cookie, and answers before anything else in
  the routing table can claim the segment.

  ## Turn off redirect following

  Bruno follows redirects by default, which would send this request on to
  example.com and hide everything worth asserting. This request carries
  `followRedirects: false` in its Settings tab; if your Bruno version predates
  that setting, turn "Follow redirects" off in the request's Settings tab by
  hand.

  ## What this costs today

  Two synchronous Postgres writes per redirect — the click row and the counter —
  which is a Principle I violation and is the point. Principle II requires the
  baseline to be measured before it is optimised, and a baseline that already
  avoids the bottleneck measures nothing. The waiver is recorded in plan.md,
  scoped to T035-T044, and expires at T045.

  Run this a few times, then re-create the link listing in a later phase to see
  `clicks_count` follow.

  Requires `linkCode`, set by `02 - Links / Create link`.
}
